<header><h1>Agendas: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/C_agendas">Agendas</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="antiintellectual-revolution"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Anti-Intellectual%20Revolution">Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When <i>Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</i> is a law in play, a player that directly gains a technology will be unaffected.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Anti-Intellectual Revolution work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;For: after you research a technology you must destroy one of your non-fighter ships.&rdquo; The trigger is researching.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player is never affected by the <i>Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</i> law.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Anti-Intellectual Revolution work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Nekro are unaffected, since Propagation gains tokens instead of researching.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> technologies count for the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; effect, whether their tokens are on another player&rsquo;s faction technology or not.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do factions start with their faction technologies &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Nekro Virus is the exception, since its two Valefar Assimilator technologies are listed as starting technologies.&rdquo; The Nekro own both Valefar Assimilator cards from the start, whether or not a token is on another technology, so each counts as a technology they own.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do technologies the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator count for objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;a copied technology counts with its colour and type.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player with no non&ndash;fighter ships on the game board may still research technology when <i>Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</i> is a law in play.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Anti-Intellectual Revolution work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It is an after-research effect, not a cost, so a player with no such ships can still research.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may only exhaust planets they control for the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; effect of <i>Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="archived-secret"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Archived%20Secret">Archived Secret</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player with three scored secret objectives may draw a fourth. However, they must immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on Impersonation at the scored-secret limit: &ldquo;you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 45.4: &ldquo;If a player has more than three secret objective cards after drawing a secret objective, they must choose one of their unscored secret objectives and return it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player draws the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Agenda_Phase:~:text=Drive%20the%20Debate"><i>Drive the Debate</i></a> secret objective while resolving <i>Archived Secret</i>, they cannot score it immediately, as the timing window to score it has already passed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Source 4 gives only the general timing: &ldquo;Secrets are scored &ldquo;after&rdquo;, so &hellip; &ldquo;Legal Text&rdquo; ACs would be played before Drive the Debate can be scored.&rdquo; The player is elected before the agenda resolves, so they did not hold the card in that window.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="armed-forces-standardization"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Armed%20Forces%20Standardization">Armed Forces Standardization</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the elected player is the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player, they choose which command tokens to remove from their fleet pool. Any other players&rsquo; command tokens removed are returned to those players&rsquo; reinforcements.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Armed Forces Standardization affect Mahact holding other players&rsquo; fleet tokens?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Mahact chooses which tokens to remove, and other players&rsquo; tokens removed go back to their owners&rsquo; reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="arms-reduction"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Arms%20Reduction">Arms Reduction</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The &ldquo;For&rdquo; outcome of Arms Reduction only affects dreadnoughts and cruisers. Afterward, if a player&rsquo;s fighters or ground forces in a space area exceed their capacity, the excess units are removed; they are not destroyed.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Arms Reduction touch ships other than dreadnoughts and cruisers &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; For only cuts dreadnoughts beyond 2 and cruisers beyond 4. Afterwards check capacity; fighters and ground forces that no longer fit are removed, which is not the same as being destroyed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="articles-of-war"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Articles%20of%20War">Articles of War</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Mechs lose all of their printed abilities other than <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a>, including <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a>, <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> and <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a>. Their cost and combat values are unchanged, including any additional dice they roll, such as for the <a href="/F_naaz_rokha">Naaz&ndash;Rokha</a> player&rsquo;s mechs.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Under Articles of War, do mechs lose Bombardment, Space Cannon and Production too?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; mechs lose all their printed abilities except Sustain Damage. Their cost and combat stats stay, so they still fight, and a mech that rolls 2 dice still does.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="checks-and-balances"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Checks%20and%20Balances">Checks and Balances</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Players choose strategy cards in the normal order, but each player gives the card they choose to another player who does not yet have their full number of strategy cards. A player keeps the card they chose only if no other player can receive it.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does strategy card selection work under Checks and Balances?&rdquo;: &ldquo;on your pick you give the card you choose to a player who doesn&rsquo;t yet have their full number of cards. Only if nobody else can take it, as for the last picker, do you keep it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the &ldquo;For&rdquo; outcome is resolved, a player who has been given a strategy card still chooses a strategy card on their turn and gives it to an eligible player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Under Checks and Balances, does a player who was given a card still pick one on their turn?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; you always pick and give away a card.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; outcome is resolved, it applies to every player, regardless of how they voted; each player readies only three of their exhausted planets, and any planets that were not exhausted remain readied.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Checks and Balances&rsquo; Against outcome work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It replaces the readying at the end of the agenda phase for everyone, however they voted: each player readies only 3 exhausted planets, and planets that weren&rsquo;t exhausted stay ready.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Public%20Disgrace"><i>Public Disgrace</i></a> action card may be played after a player has chosen a strategy card and announced which player will be receiving it. The player must choose a different strategy card, and then choose the same or a different player to receive it.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="clandestine-operations"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Clandestine%20Operations">Clandestine Operations</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the &ldquo;For&rdquo; effect of <i>Clandestine Operations</i> is resolved, the removed tokens may be from any pool or pools on a player&rsquo;s command sheet.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Clandestine Operations: &ldquo;For: Each player removes 2 command tokens from their command sheet.&rdquo; Any pool on the sheet.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="classified-document-leaks"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks">Classified Document Leaks</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If <i>Classified Document Leaks</i> is revealed when only one secret objective is in play, players may only vote for that secret objective or abstain. If no votes are cast, the speaker must decide for that secret objective to be elected.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Compare RulesPal on Judicial Abolishment: &ldquo;that law is the only eligible outcome. Abstaining isn&rsquo;t an outcome, and if nobody votes the speaker must break the 0-0 tie by choosing it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Players may still play riders if only one secret objective has been scored.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;A player may play multiple rider action cards on a single agenda.&rdquo; No exception for a single eligible outcome.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The elected objective becomes a public objective and stops being a secret objective.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;While leaked it is a public objective and no longer counts toward its owner&rsquo;s secret objectives.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Dec 2017): &ldquo;the one he originally completed now counts as public.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If there are no other secret objectives eligible to be elected by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a> revote, <i>Classified Document Leaks</i> will be discarded, and another agenda will be revealed and voted on.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The player that originally owned the secret objective elected by <i>Classified Document Leaks</i> cannot score it again after it becomes a public objective.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does a secret objective made public by Classified Document Leaks work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Nobody can score it twice, its original owner included.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Dec 2017): &ldquo;No, the objective cannot be scored a second time.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The elected secret objective no longer counts toward the original player&rsquo;s limit of three secret objectives.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;While leaked it is a public objective and no longer counts toward its owner&rsquo;s secret objectives, so they may hold another secret.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Dec 2017): &ldquo;The player whose secret objective became public can now complete another secret objective, as the one he originally completed now counts as public.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Classified Document Leaks</i> is discarded, the elected secret objective does not count toward the secret objective total of the player who originally owned it.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;it does not count toward the secret objective total of the player who originally owned it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Classified Document Leaks</i> is discarded, the elected secret objective is not returned to the original player, and it is no longer scorable as a public objective. It remains in play, not discarded, and does not count toward the original player&rsquo;s secret objective total.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;If the &lsquo;Classified Document Leaks&rsquo; agenda is discarded, what happens? A: The secret objective remains in play; it is no longer a public objective and cannot by scored by any additional players, but it does not count toward the secret objective total of the player who originally owned it.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: <sup>2</sup> Conflicts: RulesPal says &ldquo;If the law is later discarded, the card returns to its owner as a secret.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player can score a maximum of one objective of any type during or after each combat. A player cannot score the elected objective and one of their own secret objectives from the same combat.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 61.7: &ldquo;they can only score one objective during or after each combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player has their control token on the elected secret objective, they do not gain a victory point, and they cannot score it again.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What happens if a secret objective is elected as a public objective, but the Firmament has control token on it? &hellip; A: They do not gain a VP and they are unable to score it again.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="colonial-redistribution"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Colonial%20Redistribution">Colonial Redistribution</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the player that originally controlled the elected planet has the fewest victory points, they may choose themselves to place an infantry on that planet.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the elected planet has the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Demilitarized%20Zone"><i>Demilitarized Zone</i></a> exploration card attached, no infantry will be placed on it. Control of the planet will remain with the original player.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Both agendas may target the same planet. However, in that situation, infantry cannot be placed on the elected planet, so it remains under the control of its original owner.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A planet that contains neutral infantry cannot be elected, as players must cast votes for a planet that is controlled by a player.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR, Agenda Phase, Voting: &ldquo;When electing a planet, a player must cast votes for a planet that is controlled by a player.&rdquo; No player controls a planet that contains neutral infantry.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="committee-formation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Committee%20Formation">Committee Formation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Committee Formation</i> is resolved after any riders have been played, if the owner so chooses. Riders will resolve if the predicted outcome matches the player elected by the effect of <i>Committee Formation</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When is Committee Formation used, and does it combine with riders?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Just before voting, after the &lsquo;when&rsquo; and &lsquo;after&rsquo; windows, so riders are already down. &hellip; Riders that predicted the chosen player pay out.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The owner of <i>Committee Formation</i> may play riders before they resolve <i>Committee Formation</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;playing a rider and then electing that player works.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Confusing%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confusing Legal Text</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Confounding%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confounding Legal Text</i></a> action cards may be played after <i>Committee Formation</i> has been discarded to change who the elected player is, which will negate the effects of <i>Committee Formation</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Deadly%20Plot"><i>Deadly Plot</i></a> action card may be played after <i>Committee Formation</i> has been discarded to discard the agenda without resolving it, but only if that player predicted a different outcome from some other game effect.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player may own and resolve Committee Formation, even though they cannot vote.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When is Committee Formation used &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Nekro can hold and use it despite not voting.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="compensated-disarmament"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Compensated%20Disarmament">Compensated Disarmament</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>All trade goods are gained together.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Swords to Plowshares work on a planet with one infantry &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;All the trade goods from Swords to Plowshares or Compensated Disarmament arrive in a single step.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Each destroyed infantry will provide one trade good and each destroyed mech will provide one trade good.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A planet with zero units on it is eligible to be elected.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Structures are unaffected by <i>Compensated Disarmament</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Titans of <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a>&rsquo;s Hel&ndash;Titans are also ground forces and are thus affected by <i>Compensated Disarmament</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the elected planet contains coexisting units, the player that controls the planet gains all of the trade goods, including those for destroyed coexisting units.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What if a planet with coexisting units is elected via Compensated Disarmament? &hellip; A: The planet controller gains all trade goods.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="conventions-of-war"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Conventions%20of%20War">Conventions of War</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Conventions of War</i> does not prevent the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Tactical%20Bombardment"><i>Tactical Bombardment</i></a> action card or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Stellar%20Converter"><i>Stellar Converter</i></a> relic from being used on cultural planets, as neither uses the <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Restored from the original rebuild (CHANGES_REVIEW.md:1451) without the X-89 part; X-89 ΩΩ only doubles Bombardment hits. RulesPal, &ldquo;Why vote against Conventions of War&hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;For makes it a law that nobody may bombard cultural planets&rdquo;, which these cards do not do.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="core-mining" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Core%20Mining">Core Mining</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK Rulebook p. 6, &ldquo;Integrating This Expansion&rdquo;: &ldquo;remove the following agenda cards from the base game, which are no longer used when playing with the expansion: ✦ Core Mining ✦ Demilitarized Zone ✦ Holy Planet of Ixth ✦ Representative Government ✦ Research Team: Biotic ✦ Research Team: Cybernetic ✦ Research Team: Propulsion ✦ Research Team: Warfare ✦ Senate Sanctuary ✦ Shard of the Throne ✦ Terraforming Initiative ✦ The Crown of Emphidia ✦ The Crown of Thalnos&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A planet with zero infantry on it may be elected.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="covert-legislation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Covert%20Legislation">Covert Legislation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the speaker draws an agenda that would be replaced when it is revealed, such as <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a>, they follow the text of that agenda and draw a new agenda.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If Covert Legislation draws an agenda that self-replaces (e.g. miscount disclosed), does it replace immediately? A: Follow the text, draw a new agenda.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any effects that take place when or after an agenda is revealed instead take place when or after the speaker has drawn and announced the possible outcomes for the hidden agenda.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an effect, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Veto"><i>Veto</i></a> action card, would discard <i>Covert Legislation</i>, both it and the hidden agenda are discarded.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Confounding%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confounding Legal Text</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Confusing%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confusing Legal Text</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Deadly%20Plot"><i>Deadly Plot</i></a> action cards must be played before the hidden agenda is revealed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The &lsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; action cards and Deadly Plot must be played before the agenda that was voted on is revealed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The speaker may still vote on <i>Covert Legislation</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: Does the Speaker vote when Covert Legislation is drawn? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-crown-of-emphidia" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=The%20Crown%20of%20Emphidia">The Crown of Emphidia</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK Rulebook p. 6, &ldquo;Integrating This Expansion&rdquo;: &ldquo;remove the following agenda cards from the base game, which are no longer used when playing with the expansion: ✦ Core Mining ✦ Demilitarized Zone ✦ Holy Planet of Ixth ✦ Representative Government ✦ Research Team: Biotic ✦ Research Team: Cybernetic ✦ Research Team: Propulsion ✦ Research Team: Warfare ✦ Senate Sanctuary ✦ Shard of the Throne ✦ Terraforming Initiative ✦ The Crown of Emphidia ✦ The Crown of Thalnos&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>The Crown of Emphidia</i> law is discarded, no player loses a victory point.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;the player who gained a victory point from these agendas can only lose that point through the effect stated on the card. If the card is discarded in any other way, such as the &lsquo;Repeal Law&rsquo; action card, the point is not lost.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;No &mdash; a point from these laws is lost only through the condition printed on the card.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the player that gains <i>The Crown of Emphidia</i> controls no planets in their home system, they cannot lose it.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do I lose The Crown of Emphidia if I lose a planet I control in another player&rsquo;s home system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;only planets in your own home system count for it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The owner of The Crown of Emphidia only loses it if they lose control of a planet in their own home system, not a planet they control in another player&rsquo;s home system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;No &mdash; only planets in your own home system count for it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-crown-of-thalnos" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=The%20Crown%20of%20Thalnos">The Crown of Thalnos</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK Rulebook p. 6, &ldquo;Integrating This Expansion&rdquo;: &ldquo;remove the following agenda cards from the base game, which are no longer used when playing with the expansion: ✦ Core Mining ✦ Demilitarized Zone ✦ Holy Planet of Ixth ✦ Representative Government ✦ Research Team: Biotic ✦ Research Team: Cybernetic ✦ Research Team: Propulsion ✦ Research Team: Warfare ✦ Senate Sanctuary ✦ Shard of the Throne ✦ Terraforming Initiative ✦ The Crown of Emphidia ✦ The Crown of Thalnos&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Only combat rolls may be rerolled with The Crown of Thalnos; anti&ndash;fighter barrage and bombardment rolls, including those from the <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> player&rsquo;s Harrow faction ability, cannot. A player may reroll dice for units that would otherwise be destroyed, as hits are not assigned until after rolling; each unit whose rerolled die does not produce a hit is destroyed, even if its other dice produced hits.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which rolls can The Crown of Thalnos reroll?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only combat rolls, not Anti-Fighter Barrage, Bombardment (L1Z1X Harrow included) &hellip; You may reroll units that look doomed, because hits aren&rsquo;t assigned until rolling ends; any unit whose reroll fails to hit is destroyed, even if its other dice hit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="demilitarized-zone" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Demilitarized%20Zone">Demilitarized Zone</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
