<h2 id="enforced-travel-ban"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Enforced%20Travel%20Ban">Enforced Travel Ban</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of the <i>Enforced Travel Ban</i> law does not affect the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What exactly does Creuss&rsquo;s Quantum Entanglement connect &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;no game effect, Enforced Travel Ban included, can stop that.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Enforced Travel Ban</i> only prevents movement using the normal adjacency provided by wormholes. Other effects that create adjacency, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Lost%20Star%20Chart"><i>Lost Star Chart</i></a> action card, may be used to allow movement between systems containing wormholes.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Lost Star Charts during Enforced Travel Ban would more or less nullify Enforced Travel Ban in the sense that it is creating a second, separate and more extensive method of adjacency.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: <sup>2</sup> Conflicts: RulesPal, &ldquo;What does Enforced Travel Ban do&rdquo;: &ldquo;It also cancels the adjacency from Lost Star Chart for movement.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Lost Star Chart work, including with Enforced Travel Ban?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It creates its own adjacency, which a relayed FFG answer says still works under Enforced Travel Ban.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the <i>Enforced Travel Ban</i> law is in play, units cannot move through wormholes, even by effects that move ships outside of the <b>Movement</b> step of a tactical action, such as while retreating.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Where can my ships retreat to?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Under Enforced Travel Ban, alpha and beta wormholes give no adjacency for a retreat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the <i>Enforced Travel Ban</i> law is in play, the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability may still be used through wormholes.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Does the &lsquo;Enforced Travel Ban&rsquo; agenda prevent &lsquo;Space Cannon&rsquo; usage through wormholes? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;the systems stay adjacent for everything else, so Space Cannon still fires through them.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Players may still be neighbors via systems that are adjacent via wormholes.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What does Enforced Travel Ban do&rdquo;: &ldquo;the systems stay adjacent for everything else.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The &ldquo;Against&rdquo; effect of <i>Enforced Travel Ban</i> will affect PDS in or adjacent to systems containing an alpha, beta, delta or gamma wormhole.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What does Enforced Travel Ban do&rdquo;: &ldquo;Against: every PDS in or next to a system with any wormhole, gamma and delta included, is destroyed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="executive-sanctions"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Executive%20Sanctions">Executive Sanctions</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of the <i>Executive Sanctions</i> law does not affect the <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Public Execution stop the elected player voting in the next agenda phase, and does Yssaril&rsquo;s Crafty save their hand?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Crafty does beat effects that cap hand size, such as Executive Sanctions.&rdquo; Yssaril is unaffected by Executive Sanctions hand cap.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="fleet-regulations"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Fleet%20Regulations">Fleet Regulations</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When Fleet Regulations becomes a law, any command tokens in excess of four in a player&rsquo;s fleet pool are returned to their reinforcements; they cannot be moved to other pools. Any ships in excess of the new fleet pool limit are removed immediately.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When Fleet Regulations passes, what happens to fleet pool tokens above 4 and ships over the limit?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Excess fleet tokens return to reinforcements; you can&rsquo;t move them to other pools. Any ships over the new limit must be removed immediately.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The effect of the <i>Fleet Regulations</i> law does not prevent the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> player from using their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#:~:text=Armada"><sc>Armada</sc></a> faction ability. They may have up to six non&ndash;fighter ships in a system if they have four command tokens in their fleet pool.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When Fleet Regulations passes &hellip;&rdquo;: &ldquo;Abilities that raise fleet limits, like Letnev&rsquo;s, still add on top.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <i>Fleet Regulations</i> law is in play and the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player already has four command tokens in their fleet pool, they may add a fifth with their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#FAQ:~:text=Edict"><sc>Edict</sc></a> faction ability, and then choose one command token to return from their fleet pool to their reinforcements.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the law Fleet Regulations is in play, and Mahact already has 4 tokens in fleet, can they add another one &hellip;? A: The Mahact player can add a 5th token and choose one to return to their reinforcements from their fleet pool afterward.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="galactic-crisis-pact"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Galactic%20Crisis%20Pact">Galactic Crisis Pact</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If <a href="/R_leadership"><i>Leadership</i></a> is elected, players may still spend influence to gain additional command tokens when resolving its secondary ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Galactic Crisis Pact work when Leadership is elected?&rdquo;: &ldquo;there&rsquo;s no token cost to waive, but spending influence for tokens still applies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The secondary ability is resolved immediately, during the agenda phase.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Players must pay the influence or resource costs to resolve the abilities of the <a href="/R_leadership"><i>Leadership</i></a>, <a href="/R_warfare"><i>Warfare</i></a> or <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy cards if they are elected. Any planets used to pay these costs will ready at the end of the agenda phase.<sup>3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Agenda Phase: &ldquo;3. READY PLANETS Each player readies all of their planet cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card is elected, a player may exhaust a planet with a technology specialty to ignore a prerequisite on a technology as normal. This planet will ready at the end of the agenda phase.<sup>3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Agenda Phase: &ldquo;3. READY PLANETS Each player readies all of their planet cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>A player may exhaust the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#AI_Development_Algorithm"><i>AI Development Algorithm</i></a> technology to ignore a prerequisite on a unit upgrade technology as normal. <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#AI_Development_Algorithm"><i>AI Development Algorithm</i></a> will not ready at the end of the agenda phase.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a player has a strategy card in their play area due to the effect of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Political%20Stability"><i>Political Stability</i></a> action card, that strategy card is eligible to be elected.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="holy-planet-of-ixth" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Holy%20Planet%20of%20Ixth">Holy Planet of Ixth</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
