<h2 id="incentive-program"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Incentive%20Program">Incentive Program</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="ixthian-artifact"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Ixthian%20Artifact">Ixthian Artifact</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>A player may use the first technology they research to meet the prerequisites of the second technology they research.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does a technology I just researched &hellip; count as a prerequisite?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the first technology from the Technology primary counts for the second.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A player may exhaust a planet with a technology specialty to ignore a prerequisite on a technology as normal. This planet will ready at the end of the agenda phase.<sup>1,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.14: &ldquo;When researching technology, a player can exhaust a planet they control that has a technology specialty to ignore one prerequisite symbol.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Agenda Phase: &ldquo;3. READY PLANETS Each player readies all of their planet cards. Then, the agenda phase ends&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A player may exhaust the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#AI_Development_Algorithm"><i>AI Development Algorithm</i></a> technology to ignore a prerequisite on a unit upgrade technology as normal. <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#AI_Development_Algorithm"><i>AI Development Algorithm</i></a> will not ready at the end of the agenda phase.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>A player with three or fewer units in a system adjacent to the <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a> system destroys all of their units in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which units does The Ixthian Artifact destroy?&rdquo;: &ldquo;3 units of each player in every adjacent system (all of them if a player has fewer).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All units are destroyed simultaneously.<sup>1,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Units destroyed by &lsquo;Ixthian Artifact&rsquo; are destroyed simultaneously.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Clipper, Sep 2018): &ldquo;the intent is that the ancient artifact explosions should happen simultaneously.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quantum%20Entanglement"><sc>Quantum Entanglement</sc></a> faction ability does not make any additional systems adjacent to the Mecatol Rex system for the purposes of <i>Ixthian Artifact</i>.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;If there is an &lsquo;A&rsquo; wormhole on Mecatol Rex when the &lsquo;Ixthian Artifact&rsquo; agenda causes units in adjacent systems to be destroyed, does the Quantum Entanglement ability cause the Ghost of Creuss faction to lose units in a system that contains a &lsquo;B&rsquo; wormhole? A: No. Only the Creuss treats those systems as adjacent.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which units does The Ixthian Artifact destroy?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Adjacency is the normal kind for everyone: a matching wormhole on Mecatol counts, but Creuss&rsquo;s Quantum Entanglement doesn&rsquo;t extend it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Flagship:~:text=Hil%20Colish"><i>Hil Colish</i></a>, is in the Mecatol Rex system, the Creuss home system and the Creuss Gate system are adjacent to it, as each contains a delta wormhole. Units in those systems will be affected.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which units does The Ixthian Artifact destroy?&rdquo;: &ldquo;a matching wormhole on Mecatol counts&rdquo; The Hil Colish puts a delta wormhole in its system.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li class="ixth">To cast votes against or to play a rider on <i>Ixthian Artifact</i> is to commit heresy.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="judicial-abolishment"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Judicial%20Abolishment">Judicial Abolishment</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If <i>Judicial Abolishment</i> is revealed when only one law is in play, players may only vote for that law or abstain. If no votes are cast, the speaker must decide for that law to be elected.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If Judicial Abolishment comes up with only one law in play, can that law be saved?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; that law is the only eligible outcome. Abstaining isn&rsquo;t an outcome, and if nobody votes the speaker must break the 0-0 tie by choosing it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Players may still play riders if only one law is in play.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;A player may play multiple rider action cards on a single agenda.&rdquo; No exception for a single eligible outcome.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-antiquities"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Methods_of_Acquiring_Relics:~:text=Minister%20of%20Antiquities">Minister of Antiquities</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-commerce"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Commerce">Minister of Commerce</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Minister of Commerce</i> triggers when its owner has their commodities replenished by any game effect.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do Minister of Commerce, Industry, Peace and War interact &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Minister of Commerce still pays 1 trade good per neighbor when your commodities were already full, since you still replenished.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Gaining a fixed number of commodities does not trigger <i>Minister of Commerce</i>, even if doing so would result in its owner having commodities equal to their commodity value.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The owner of Minister of Commerce gains trade goods from Minister of Commerce when they replenish commodities, even if they already have their maximum number of commodities.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Minister of Commerce still pays 1 trade good per neighbor when your commodities were already full, since you still replenished.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All trade goods are gained together.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Swords to Plowshares work on a planet with one infantry &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;All the trade goods from Swords to Plowshares or Compensated Disarmament arrive in a single step.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-exploration"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Exploration">Minister of Exploration</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the owner of <i>Minister of Exploration</i> gains control of multiple planets during one invasion, the trade goods are gained one at a time.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-industry"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Industry">Minister of Industry</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>All units in that system may use their <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability, not just the placed space dock.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Minister of Industry lets you produce in that system right after placing the dock.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The produced units must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When an ability other than &lsquo;Production&rsquo; allows you to produce one or more units, do you have to pay for the units produced? A: Yes, a unit that is produced must always be paid for.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What can Integrated Economy produce?&rdquo;: &ldquo;up to the new planet&rsquo;s resource value in cost, paid normally.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A space dock cannot be placed on a planet already containing a space dock.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 85.4: &ldquo;A player can have a maximum of one space dock on each planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If a player has no space docks in their reinforcements when they may place a space dock on the game board, they may first remove a space dock from a system that does not contain their command token.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 24.4a: &ldquo;If a player does not have the unit in their reinforcements, that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>An ability that puts a space dock on the game board by &ldquo;replacing&rdquo;, rather than &ldquo;placing&rdquo;, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Infiltrate"><i>Infiltrate</i></a> action card, will trigger <i>Minister of Industry</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any instance of &lsquo;replace&rsquo; can be considered to say &lsquo;remove and place&rsquo; if no units are left in reinforcements &hellip; Note, this overturns a previous ruling regarding Minister of Industry.&rdquo; Overturns the Oct 3, 2018 ruling (source 5 line 1457).</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Moving the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> into a system is not placing a space dock, and does not trigger Minister of Industry.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What triggers Minister of Industry?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A Saar Floating Factory moving into a system doesn&rsquo;t trigger it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-peace"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Peace">Minister of Peace</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Once a player resolves the ability of <i>Minister of Peace</i>, the active player cannot use any &ldquo;after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When is Minister of Peace used &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Once it ends the active player&rsquo;s turn, no other abilities in that window can be resolved, per the developer&rsquo;s later FAQ ruling.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Other players, including the <i>Minister of Peace</i> player, cannot use any &ldquo;after another player activates a system that&hellip;&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;no other abilities in that window can be resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The active player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities when their turn is ended by <i>Minister of Peace</i>.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;A previous ruling has stated that if an effect ends a player&rsquo;s turn, they may still use &lsquo;at the end of your turn&rsquo; abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The player that owns <i>Minister of Peace</i> does not have to have any of their units in the active system to resolve <i>Minister of Peace</i>, so long as any non&ndash;active player owns at least one unit in the active system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do Minister of Commerce, Industry, Peace and War interact &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Minister of Peace&rsquo;s owner needn&rsquo;t have units in the activated system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-policy"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Policy">Minister of Policy</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The owner of <i>Minister of Policy</i> will draw action cards during the <b>Draw Action Cards</b> step of the status phase, and again at the end of the status phase.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player owns <i>Minister of Policy</i>, they will use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yssaril_Tribes#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Scheming"><sc>Scheming</sc></a> ability for both the <b>Draw Action Cards</b> step and for <i>Minister of Policy</i>.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;The Yssaril&rsquo;s &lsquo;Scheming&rsquo; ability, however, is triggered each time that action cards are drawn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#Neural_Motivator"><i>Neural Motivator</i></a> does not apply when the owner of <i>Minister of Policy</i> draws action cards from its effect.<sup>1,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Neural Motivator&rsquo; gives only one action card in addition to the standard status phase draw. It is not triggered additional times by other abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Mar 2019): &ldquo;NM is intended to refer to the specific step of the status phase, not a blanket rule. I can see the reasoning there, but no.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-sciences"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Sciences">Minister of Sciences</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="minister-of-war"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20War">Minister of War</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Performing any action is the trigger for the remainder of the ability of <i>Minister of War</i>.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Is the trigger for the &lsquo;Minister of War&rsquo; agenda card&rsquo;s ability &lsquo;performing an action&rsquo;? A: Yes. Performing any action is the trigger for the remainder of the &lsquo;Minister of War&rsquo; agenda card&rsquo;s ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Minister of War be used after any action?&rdquo;: &ldquo;its owner can discard it after any action &hellip; it doesn&rsquo;t need to follow an action that removed a token.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Mattchew222, Feb 6, 2018): &ldquo;You can discard the Minister of War card after doing ANY action to take an additional action.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Resolving Minister of War is not an action. As such, a player with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Fleet_Logistics"><i>Fleet Logistics</i></a> technology may perform three actions in one turn.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do Minister of Commerce, Industry, Peace and War interact &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Minister of War isn&rsquo;t an action itself, so with Fleet Logistics you can take three actions in a turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Effects that trigger at the start or end of a player&rsquo;s turn will not trigger between each of those player&rsquo;s actions.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="miscount-disclosed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed">Miscount Disclosed</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If <i>Miscount Disclosed</i> is revealed when only one law is in play, players may only vote for that law or abstain. If no votes are cast, the speaker must decide for that law to be elected.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Compare RulesPal on Judicial Abolishment: &ldquo;that law is the only eligible outcome &hellip; if nobody votes the speaker must break the 0-0 tie by choosing it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Players may still play riders if only one law is in play.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;A player may play multiple rider action cards on a single agenda.&rdquo; No exception for a single eligible outcome.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The elected law remains in play while it is being voted on.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When Miscount Disclosed forces a revote on a law, does that law stay in effect during the revote?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; the law remains in play until the revote resolves.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;the law that is being voted on because of &lsquo;Miscount Disclosed&rsquo; remains in play during the revote.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Committee%20Formation"><i>Committee Formation</i></a> is elected by <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, the owner may use its ability. The elected player will receive <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Committee%20Formation"><i>Committee Formation</i></a> from the discard pile.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Political%20Censure"><i>Political Censure</i></a> is elected by <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, the current owner cannot play action cards, including <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Confounding%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confounding Legal Text</i></a>, if another player is elected. If another player is elected, that player may play the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Confusing%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confusing Legal Text</i></a> action card.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Representative%20Government"><i>Representative Government</i></a> is elected by <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, each player will cast only one vote during the revote.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;the law remains in play until the revote resolves, so Representative Government, for example, still limits everyone to 1 vote.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Once the law is elected, any riders on <i>Miscount Disclosed</i> will resolve. Following that, the elected law is then treated as being revealed.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the revote from Miscount Disclosed work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;First vote on Miscount Disclosed, with riders predicting only which law is chosen. Then vote on that law as if it had just been revealed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks"><i>Classified Document Leaks</i></a> is elected by <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, and there are no other secret objectives eligible to be elected by the <i>Miscount Disclosed</i> revote, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks"><i>Classified Document Leaks</i></a> will be discarded and replaced.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>When the elected law is treated as revealed, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Veto"><i>Veto</i></a> action card or the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quash"><sc>Quash</sc></a> faction ability may be played. If so, the law will be discarded and replaced.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;vote on that law as if it had just been revealed, so Veto, Quash and a fresh round of riders can be played on it.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Yes, the other Agenda can be Quashed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>After the elected law is treated as revealed, riders may be played to predict the outcome of the elected law.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;so Veto, Quash and a fresh round of riders can be played on it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Planets are not readied between the vote on Miscount Disclosed and the vote on the elected law. The vote on the elected law does not replace the second agenda of the agenda phase, so three agendas may be voted on during that agenda phase.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Planets are not readied in between, and the revote doesn&rsquo;t replace the phase&rsquo;s second agenda, so a phase can have three votes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>After all players have voted for <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Deadly%20Plot"><i>Deadly Plot</i></a> action card may be played. If so, the elected law is not voted on and remains in play.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>After all players have voted for the elected law, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Deadly%20Plot"><i>Deadly Plot</i></a> action card may be played. If so, the elected law is discarded.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Players who resolved a transaction while voting on and resolving <i>Miscount Disclosed</i> may resolve an additional transaction voting on and resolving the elected law.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling, asked whether Miscount Disclosed &ldquo;refresh[es] the &lsquo;transaction allowance&rsquo;&rdquo;: &ldquo;I would also say that they could perform new transactions.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li class="removed">If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Holy%20Planet%20of%20Ixth"><i>Holy Planet of Ixth</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Shard%20of%20the%20Throne"><i>Shard of the Throne</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=The%20Crown%20of%20Emphidia"><i>The Crown of Emphidia</i></a> is elected by <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, the previous owner keeps their victory point, and the newly elected owner gains a victory point, even if they were also the previous owner.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If Shard of the Throne, The Crown of Emphidia or Holy Planet of Ixth is discarded or re-elected &hellip;&rdquo;: &ldquo;If the law is discarded some other way, such as Repeal Law, or re-elected via Miscount Disclosed, the old owner keeps the point; a newly elected owner gains one, and the same player re-elected scores again.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the VP from the original Agenda is now permanently associated with the player who had it when the law was re-voted on, and that the &ldquo;new&rdquo; card is now worth a second VP that functions as normal.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Because the losing of the victory points is tied to the combat and not the losing of the card, the former owner would keep the victory point in both cases.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="mutiny"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Mutiny">Mutiny</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Whichever outcome of <i>Mutiny</i> is resolved, players gain or lose victory points in speaker order.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="new-constitution"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=New%20Constitution">New Constitution</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player controls planets in another player&rsquo;s home system, those planets are not exhausted by the &ldquo;For&rdquo; outcome of <i>New Constitution</i>.<sup>2,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: Does New Constitution exhaust home planets if they&rsquo;re not controlled by their owner? A: No, you only exhaust planets in your home system if you control them.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;A New Constitution only exhausts the planets each player controls in their own home system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;each player exhausts each planet in his home system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nexus-sovereignty"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Nexus%20Sovereignty">Nexus Sovereignty</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of the <i>Nexus Sovereignty</i> law does not affect the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the <i>Nexus Sovereignty</i> law is in play, units cannot move through the alpha and beta wormholes in the wormhole nexus, even by effects that move ships outside of the movement step of a tactical action, such as while retreating.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the <i>Nexus Sovereignty</i> law is in play, hits may still be produced against ships in the active system by units with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/PDS#Upgraded_Unit:~:text=Deep%20Space%20Cannon"><sc>Deep Space Cannon</sc></a> ability in systems that are adjacent via a wormhole during the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step of a tactical action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Players may still be neighbors via systems that are adjacent via wormholes.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What does Enforced Travel Ban do&rdquo;: &ldquo;the systems stay adjacent for everything else.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="political-censure"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Political%20Censure">Political Censure</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When a player is elected for <i>Political Censure</i>, they may play the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Confusing%20Legal%20Text"><i>Confusing Legal Text</i></a> action card before it resolves.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do Confusing and Confounding Legal Text interact &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;only the player originally elected can play them. They act before the outcome resolves.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Political Censure</i> is elected by <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a>, the previous owner loses one victory point when they lose the card, and the newly elected player gains one victory point. If the same player is elected again, they lose and then regain the victory point.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If Miscount Disclosed revotes Political Censure, who gains or loses points?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the previous owner loses 1 and the new owner gains 1; the same player re-elected loses and regains it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>While <i>Political Censure</i> is being voted on again, it remains in play, so its current owner still cannot play action cards until the vote has resolved.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Q: During a revote initiated by the &ldquo;Miscount Disclosed&rdquo; agenda, does the law that is being voted on remain active and in play? A: Yes, the law that is being voted on because of &ldquo;Miscount Disclosed&rdquo; remains in play during the revote.&rdquo; Political Censure stays in play, so its effect on the current owner continues.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When Miscount Disclosed forces a revote on a law, does that law stay in effect during the revote?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; the law remains in play until the revote resolves, so Representative Government, for example, still limits everyone to 1 vote.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li><i>Political Censure</i> only prevents the elected player from playing action cards; it does not affect strategy cards. The elected player cannot discard <i>Political Censure</i> themselves.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What does Political Censure stop, and how is it removed?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only playing action cards; strategy cards are unaffected. The elected player can&rsquo;t discard it themselves.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="prophecy-of-ixth"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Prophecy%20of%20Ixth">Prophecy of Ixth</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Other effects that produce units without a unit using its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability will not cause <i>Prophecy of Ixth</i> to be discarded.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does producing with Sling Relay trigger the Prophecy of Ixth drawback?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; it only applies when you use a unit&rsquo;s Production ability, which Sling Relay doesn&rsquo;t.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="public-execution"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Public%20Execution">Public Execution</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player&rsquo;s Crafty faction ability does not prevent them from discarding their action cards if they are elected by Public Execution, as the discard is not caused by the hand limit.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Public Execution &hellip;, and does Yssaril&rsquo;s Crafty save their hand?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The discard comes from being elected, not from the hand limit, so Yssaril must discard too.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Public Execution</i> is resolved during the action phase, such as with the <a href="/F_keleres">Keleres</a> <i>Executive Order</i> technology, the elected player may still vote in the following agenda phase.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;After the Xxcha hero resolves agendas in the action phase, do exhausted planets stay exhausted, and does Public Execution carry over?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A player elected for Public Execution can still vote in the next agenda phase.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Public Execution stop the elected player voting in the next agenda phase &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The voting ban only covers that agenda phase.&rdquo; Neither names Executive Order; it also resolves an agenda outside the agenda phase.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="publicize-weapon-schematics"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Publicize%20Weapon%20Schematics">Publicize Weapon Schematics</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the <i>Publicize Weapon Schematics</i> law is in play, and a player is the first to gain the war sun unit upgrade technology, from then on, prerequisites for the war sun unit upgrade technology will be ignored.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> does not own their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#FAQ:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> II faction unit upgrade technology, they do not own a war sun technology.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Do pre-printed units count as &lsquo;technologies&rsquo;? Specifically, does Prototype War Sun I count as a technology? &hellip; Dane: They do not. Preprinted units do not count as technologies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the <i>Publicize Weapon Schematics</i> law is in play, the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player will not cause prerequisites for the War Sun unit upgrade technology to be ignored if they do not own their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#FAQ:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> II faction unit upgrade technology.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;Preprinted units do not count as technologies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; outcome of <i>Publicize Weapon Schematics</i> is resolved, the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player will not discard their action cards if they do not own their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#FAQ:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> II faction unit upgrade technology.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Same ruling, which asked whether it &ldquo;count[s] against the &lsquo;Against&rsquo; effects of Publicize Weapons Schematics&rdquo;: &ldquo;They do not.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#FAQ:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> will lose its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, regardless of if the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player owns their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#FAQ:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> II faction unit upgrade technology.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has copied a faction&ndash;specific war sun unit upgrade technology with <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a>, they own a war sun technology for the purposes of <i>Publicize Weapon Schematics</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What can the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Faction technology cards another player has actually researched, unit upgrades included.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="rearmament-agreement"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Rearmament%20Agreement">Rearmament Agreement</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player that controls no planets in their home system will not place a mech if the &ldquo;For&rdquo; outcome of Rearmament Agreement is resolved.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player that has no mechs on the game board is unaffected by the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; effect of Rearmament Agreement.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

