<h2 id="research-grant-reallocation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Research%20Grant%20Reallocation">Research Grant Reallocation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player may gain any technology, regardless of the number of command tokens in their fleet pool.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If a player must remove more command tokens than they have in their fleet pool, they remove all their command tokens from their fleet pool instead.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The number and colors of technologies a player owns will have no effect on the number of command tokens they remove.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>A player cannot exhaust a planet with a technology specialty to reduce the number of command tokens they remove.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="research-team-biotic" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Research%20Team%3A%20Biotic">Research Team: Biotic</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK Rulebook p. 6, &ldquo;Integrating This Expansion&rdquo;: &ldquo;remove the following agenda cards from the base game, which are no longer used when playing with the expansion: ✦ Core Mining ✦ Demilitarized Zone ✦ Holy Planet of Ixth ✦ Representative Government ✦ Research Team: Biotic ✦ Research Team: Cybernetic ✦ Research Team: Propulsion ✦ Research Team: Warfare ✦ Senate Sanctuary ✦ Shard of the Throne ✦ Terraforming Initiative ✦ The Crown of Emphidia ✦ The Crown of Thalnos&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The agenda card, not the planet, is exhausted to ignore the prerequisite.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When a &lsquo;Research Team&rsquo; agenda that is attached to a planet is used to ignore a prerequisite, is the planet exhausted? A: No. The agenda is exhausted, not the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do the Research Team agendas work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You exhaust the Research Team card, not the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The elected planet does not gain a technology specialty, and does not count as a planet with a technology specialty for objectives.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do the Research Team agendas work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;They don&rsquo;t give the planet a technology specialty, so they don&rsquo;t count for objectives about specialty planets.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

