<h2 id="search-warrant"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Search%20Warrant">Search Warrant</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player with three scored secret objectives may draw a fourth. However, they must immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on drawing past the scored-secret limit: &ldquo;you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 45.4: &ldquo;If a player has more than three secret objective cards after drawing a secret objective, they must choose one of their unscored secret objectives and return it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the elected player has three secret objective cards, and they would draw another, the drawn secret objective card is revealed before that player chooses which card to discard. This applies both when the elected player initially draws the secret objective cards from the effect of <i>Search Warrant</i> when they are elected, and if they later draw secret objective cards from another effect.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player draws the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Agenda_Phase:~:text=Drive%20the%20Debate"><i>Drive the Debate</i></a> secret objective while resolving <i>Search Warrant</i>, they cannot score it immediately, as the timing window to score it has already passed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Source 4 gives only the general timing: &ldquo;Secrets are scored &ldquo;after&rdquo;, so &hellip; &ldquo;Legal Text&rdquo; ACs would be played before Drive the Debate can be scored.&rdquo; The player is elected before the agenda resolves, so they did not hold the card in that window.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="seed-of-an-empire"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Seed%20of%20an%20Empire">Seed of an Empire</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If multiple players have the most or fewest victory points, they gain victory points in speaker order.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If players are tied for the most or fewest points when Seed of an Empire resolves, who scores?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Every tied player gains the point. Effects aimed at the player with the most or fewest points hit everyone tied; the speaker doesn&rsquo;t break this kind of tie.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When several players are tied for the most or fewest victory points &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;All of them &mdash; every tied player counts.&rdquo; Order is not addressed.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="senate-sanctuary" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Senate%20Sanctuary">Senate Sanctuary</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK Rulebook p. 6, &ldquo;Integrating This Expansion&rdquo;: &ldquo;remove the following agenda cards from the base game, which are no longer used when playing with the expansion: ✦ Core Mining ✦ Demilitarized Zone ✦ Holy Planet of Ixth ✦ Representative Government ✦ Research Team: Biotic ✦ Research Team: Cybernetic ✦ Research Team: Propulsion ✦ Research Team: Warfare ✦ Senate Sanctuary ✦ Shard of the Throne ✦ Terraforming Initiative ✦ The Crown of Emphidia ✦ The Crown of Thalnos&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="shard-of-the-throne" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Shard%20of%20the%20Throne">Shard of the Throne</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK Rulebook p. 6, &ldquo;Integrating This Expansion&rdquo;: &ldquo;remove the following agenda cards from the base game, which are no longer used when playing with the expansion: ✦ Core Mining ✦ Demilitarized Zone ✦ Holy Planet of Ixth ✦ Representative Government ✦ Research Team: Biotic ✦ Research Team: Cybernetic ✦ Research Team: Propulsion ✦ Research Team: Warfare ✦ Senate Sanctuary ✦ Shard of the Throne ✦ Terraforming Initiative ✦ The Crown of Emphidia ✦ The Crown of Thalnos&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <i>Shard of the Throne</i> law is discarded, no player loses a victory point.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;the player who gained a victory point from these agendas can only lose that point through the effect stated on the card.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;No &mdash; a point from these laws is lost only through the condition printed on the card.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the former owner would keep the victory point in both cases.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Shard of the Throne does not change hands if a combat ends in a draw, or if no combat occurs, such as when ground forces land on a planet without opposing ground forces or the Bombardment ability destroys the last defending ground forces.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Shard of the Throne change hands if both sides&rsquo; ground forces are wiped out?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; if neither player has ground forces left, nobody won the combat, so the Shard stays put. It also never moves through combats that don&rsquo;t happen, such as landing unopposed or bombarding the last defenders.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="shared-research"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Shared%20Research">Shared Research</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; outcome is resolved, a player with no command tokens in their reinforcements does not place one. They do not take a command token from their command sheet.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No numbered source. RulesPal, &ldquo;Under Shared Research&rsquo;s Against outcome, what if I have no command tokens in reinforcements?&rdquo; (graded Best reading, unconfirmed; not used): &ldquo;Then you place nothing &mdash; the outcome places a token only if able, so you don&rsquo;t take one from your sheet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="swords-to-plowshares"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Swords%20to%20Plowshares">Swords to Plowshares</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a planet contains only one infantry, that infantry is destroyed and its owner gains one trade good. All trade goods from Swords to Plowshares are gained together, so the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may use their Pillage faction ability on each affected neighbor only once.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Swords to Plowshares work on a planet with one infantry &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Half of one rounded up is one, so the lone infantry is destroyed and you gain 1 trade good. All the trade goods from Swords to Plowshares or Compensated Disarmament arrive in a single step, so Mentak can pillage each affected neighbor only once.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Mechs are ignored by the &ldquo;For&rdquo; effect of <i>Swords to Plowshares</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Neutral infantry are unaffected by <i>Swords to Plowshares</i>, as there is no neutral player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

